<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nasr al-Dawla ibn Marwan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1011–1061</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Nasr al-Dawla Ahmad ibn Marwan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nasr al-Dawla Ahmad ibn Marwan was the Kurdish Marwanid ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diyar-bakr">Diyar Bakr</a> from 1011 to 1061, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mayyafariqin">Mayyafariqin</a>. During his fifty-year reign he kept peace with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimids</a> and the rising <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuks</a> through diplomacy and gifts. His capital gained mosques, a hospital and bridges, and attracted scholars and refugees from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a>.</p></div>
